Add a trusted-LAN HTTP foundation for the Wi-Fi variants of the Aliro
door-lock reader firmware.

This patch is applied only to the Wi-Fi variants (nanoc6-wifi and
atoms3-lite-wifi); the Thread variant never applies, compiles, links
or starts any of the code introduced here.

Scope:
  * new main/aliro_local_web.h and main/aliro_local_web.cpp implementing
    a native esp_http_server on the Matter Wi-Fi station;
  * three read-only routes: GET /, GET /api/status, GET /api/pairing;
  * server lifecycle tied to IP_EVENT_STA_GOT_IP / _LOST_IP and
    WIFI_EVENT_STA_DISCONNECTED so it is only up while the station has
    a valid assigned IP; failure is logged and swallowed;
  * one call from app_main() that registers the lifecycle handler after
    Matter start.

Explicit non-goals for this patch: no Arduino runtime, no LittleFS,
no captive AP, no TLS/SSL, no authentication, no compiled-in Wi-Fi
credentials, no settings / logs / reboot / factory-reset / OTA /
WebSocket endpoints. Trusted-LAN HTTP is intentional.

